# Paths under the project root that travel between this clone and the VM's
# persistent data disk. scripts/gce-push.sh and scripts/gce-pull.sh sync these,
# one file at a time:
#   - push creates files missing on the VM, and replaces an existing VM file
#     only when it is named with --overwrite <path> and its VM copy is unchanged
#     since the last sync; it never deletes
#   - pull replaces local files the VM changed since the last sync
#
# Runtime-owned paths (data/state, data/sessions, data/repositories, …) are
# rejected here: the running bot owns them.
#
# Copy this file to data/.deploy-include (gitignored) and edit it to match
# your instance:
#   cp data/.deploy-include.example data/.deploy-include
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the repo root. Lines starting with
# `#` and blank lines are ignored.

# Universal project-class paths (every Clack instance should list these)
data/config.json
data/mcp.json
data/default_configuration

# Operator-provided worker guardrails (see docs/worker-settings.md); a path
# that doesn't exist locally is simply skipped.
data/worker-settings.json

# Per-instance project paths — uncomment / add lines below as needed.
# Plugins that ship code (an index.js + assets, no persistent state) go here.
# Plugins that keep state on the VM (e.g. trivia's question/score JSON) must
# NOT be listed: their files change on the VM between syncs.
#
# Examples:
# data/plugins/my-org-plugin
# data/plugins/another-code-only-plugin
